WEBVTT

00:00:00.797 --> 00:00:03.768
Meet MXI RoboICL.

00:00:04.034 --> 00:00:06.632
Can a robot learn better actions simply by

00:00:06.632 --> 00:00:09.470
watching examples, and remembering what happened?

00:00:10.595 --> 00:00:12.262
Start with one demonstration.

00:00:12.532 --> 00:00:14.991
Sample short windows across its timeline,

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.390
so the model can see how the task unfolds.

00:00:18.085 --> 00:00:22.005
Open a window: an observation, a sequence of actions,

00:00:22.238 --> 00:00:25.381
an execution receipt, and the resulting observation.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:28.757
The current episode grows in the same format.

00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:32.768
Each completed action adds another piece of experience.

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.292
Keep earlier time anchors and the latest segment.

00:00:36.556 --> 00:00:39.438
Send that memory, the demonstration, and

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:41.352
the current observation to the agent.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.258
The agent chooses its next action.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.457
The outcome comes back as context.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.258
No model weights change.

00:00:50.595 --> 00:00:52.329
The robot sees the object.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:55.403
But where, exactly, will its fingers close?

00:00:55.663 --> 00:00:56.958
Look at this raw wrist view.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.095
The camera is already there.

00:00:59.363 --> 00:01:01.800
Our addition projects the gripper's grasp

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.695
center and inner edges into the image.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.020
Now the offset is visible.

00:01:08.312 --> 00:01:12.070
As the hand approaches, watch the tube move toward the guide.

00:01:13.084 --> 00:01:14.696
Align, close, and lift.

00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:16.501
The marker guides alignment.

00:01:16.778 --> 00:01:19.473
The object's motion confirms that the grasp held.

00:01:20.592 --> 00:01:22.634
This is a recorded pouring task.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.981
The robot must locate the vase mouth, not just recognize the vase.

00:01:27.612 --> 00:01:29.833
Freeze the same moment across cameras.

00:01:30.112 --> 00:01:33.495
Match the same landmark in the head and left wrist views.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.302
One pixel leaves distance unknown.

00:01:37.557 --> 00:01:40.197
Two calibrated rays recover a three-dimensional

00:01:40.197 --> 00:01:42.287
position, without a depth map.

00:01:43.088 --> 00:01:45.308
Depth resolves to about half a metre.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.150
The right wrist is occluded, so only

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.195
the two matching views contribute.

00:01:51.088 --> 00:01:52.658
Now follow the real motion.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:55.350
The logged lip-to-mouth offset shrinks from

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.732
seventy-eight to three millimetres, before the pour.

00:02:00.588 --> 00:02:05.333
The planner turns a destination into motion the arm can execute.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.083
Watch this recorded episode.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.645
The first preview fails.

00:02:09.925 --> 00:02:12.595
Inverse kinematics finds no complete route.

00:02:12.862 --> 00:02:13.983
The robot waits.

00:02:15.095 --> 00:02:16.348
Another plan passes.

00:02:16.622 --> 00:02:19.150
The tool selects the left arm and estimates

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.559
five hundred and ten steps, without moving.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.468
The motion connects intermediate poses and joint targets.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.241
These values come from recorded commands.

00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:34.485
Now the real arm executes: grasp, lift, transfer, align, and pour.

00:02:35.094 --> 00:02:36.394
Task score: one hundred.

00:02:36.639 --> 00:02:39.578
A later return-home warning remains in the log.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.375
The interface stays compact: roughly

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:45.570
six thousand audited characters.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.832
Experience comes through context.

00:02:49.088 --> 00:02:53.370
In three exploratory task groups, removing readable task

00:02:53.775 --> 00:02:57.095
and scene priors caused smaller score drops than Q0.

00:02:59.081 --> 00:03:02.664
Our current self-evaluation reaches seventy-five point nine.

00:03:02.913 --> 00:03:04.945
A simple foundation, with clearer

00:03:04.945 --> 00:03:07.386
geometry and more deliberate execution.

00:03:32.433 --> 00:03:33.616
RoboICL.

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:35.516
Learning through context.

00:03:35.821 --> 00:03:36.741
Thank you for watching.
